ment":"","startLine":60,"endLine":77,"calleeNames":["is_List"]},"acm000006383jsd":{"type":"ControlElement","id":"acm000006383jsd","name":"_do_add","comment":"","startLine":79,"endLine":108,"calleeNames":["Variable","is_List","is_Tuple","list","is_valid_construction_var","UserError","str","append"]},"acm000006384jsd":{"type":"ControlElement","id":"acm000006384jsd","name":"keys","comment":"Returns the keywords for the options.","startLine":110,"endLine":112,"calleeNames":[]},"acm000006385jsd":{"type":"ControlElement","id":"acm000006385jsd","name":"Add","comment":"","startLine":114,"endLine":140,"calleeNames":["is_List","is_Tuple","len","_do_add"]},"acm000006386jsd":{"type":"ControlElement","id":"acm000006386jsd","name":"AddVariables","comment":"Adds a list of options. Each list element is a tuple/list of arguments to be passed on to the underlying method for adding options. Example:: opt.AddVariables( ('debug', '', 0), ('CC', 'The C compiler'), ('VALIDATE', 'An option for testing validation', 'notset', validator, None), )","startLine":142,"endLine":159,"calleeNames":["_do_add"]},"acm000006387jsd":{"type":"ControlElement","id":"acm000006387jsd","name":"Update","comment":"Updates an environment with the option variables. Args: env: the environment to update. args (optional): a dictionary of keys and values to update in *env*. If omitted, uses the variables from the commandline.","startLine":161,"endLine":230,"calleeNames":["exists","split","abspath","insert","open","read","exec","items","subst","converter","UserError","validator"]},"acm000006388jsd":{"type":"ControlElement","id":"acm000006388jsd","name":"UnknownVariables","comment":"Returns unknown variables. Identifies options that were not known, declared options in this object.","startLine":232,"endLine":237,"calleeNames":[]},"acm000006389jsd":{"type":"ControlElement","id":"acm000006389jsd","name":"Save","comment":"Save the options to a file. Saves all the options which have non-default settings to the given file as Python expressions. This file can then be used to load the options for a subsequent run. This can be used to create an option cache file. Args: filename: Name of the file to save into env: the environment get the option values from\nCreate the file and write out the header\nMake an assignment in the file for each option\nwithin the environment that was assigned a value\nother than the default. We don't want to save the\nones set to default: in case the SConscript settings\nchange you would then pick up old defaults.\nConvert stuff that has a repr() that\ncannot be evaluated into a string","startLine":239,"endLine":289,"calleeNames":["open","eval","repr","to_String","prepare","subst","converter","str","write","UserError"]},"acm000006390jsd":{"type":"ControlElement","id":"acm000006390jsd","name":"GenerateHelpText","comment":"Generates the help text for the options. Args: env: an environment that is used to get the current values of the options. sort: Either a comparison function used for sorting (must take two arguments and return -1, 0 or 1) or a boolean to indicate if it should be sorted.","startLine":291,"endLine":317,"calleeNames":["callable","sorted","cmp_to_key","sort","subst","FormatVariableHelpText","map","join"]},"acm000006391jsd":{"type":"ControlElement","id":"acm000006391jsd","name":"FormatVariableHelpText","comment":"Don't display the key name itself as an alias.","startLine":322,"endLine":330,"calleeNames":[]},"acm000006392jsd":{"type":"ClassUnit","id":"acm000006392jsd","name":"Variables","comment":"Holds all the options, updates the environment with the variables, and renders the help text. If *is_global* is true, this is a singleton, create only once. Args: files (optional): List of option configuration files to load (backward compatibility). If a single string is passed it is automatically placed in a file list (Default value = None) args (optional): dictionary to override values set from *files*. (Default value = None) is_global (optional): global ins